LeetCode 1545: Find Kth Bit in Nth Binary String
1. Problem Understanding
We are given a sequence of binary strings defined as:
S1 = "0"
Si = S(i-1) + "1" + reverse(invert(S(i-1)))

Our task is to find the kth bit (1-indexed) in Sn.
2. Key Observations
• Length of Sn = 2^n - 1
• Middle position = 2^(n-1)
• Structure:
  Left  -> S(n-1)
  Middle -> '1'
  Right -> reverse(invert(S(n-1)))
3. Core Logic
Instead of building the entire string (which grows exponentially), we use recursion and pattern observation.

Case 1: If k equals middle position → return '1'
Case 2: If k is in left half → same as findKthBit(n-1, k)
Case 3: If k is in right half →
    - Mirror index: new_k = length - k + 1
    - Recursively find bit at (n-1, new_k)
    - Invert the result
4. Methodology (Step-by-Step)
Step 1: Define base case → If n == 1, return '0'
Step 2: Compute length = 2^n - 1
Step 3: Compute mid = (length // 2) + 1
Step 4: Compare k with mid and apply cases
Step 5: Use recursion to reduce the problem size
5. Why This Approach Works
The string has a symmetric structure. The right half is just the reversed and inverted version of the left half. This allows us to avoid constructing the full string and instead reduce the problem recursively.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(n) due to recursion stack
6. Concepts Used
• Recursion
• Divide and Conquer
• Mathematical Pattern Recognition
• Bit Manipulation (2^n using bit shifting)
• Symmetry in Binary Structures

